        {
          "id": "when-to-worry-about-ticking",
          "title": "⚠️ When to worry about ticking",
          "description": "Ticking is usually harmless - but these are warning signs:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Ticking persists after oil is topped up or changed",
                "Ticking gets louder or increases with RPM",
                "Ticking is accompanied by: oil pressure warning light, loss of power, rough idle, or engine warning light"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "If any of the above apply, book a diagnostic immediately (£50-£150)."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Book Diagnostic"
            },
            {
              "type": "cards",
              "cards": [
                {
                  "title": "What happens if you ignore it",
                  "text": "The £5,000 mistake: Ignoring a ticking noise for just a few more weeks can turn a £60 oil change into a £10,000 engine replacement.",
                  "highlight": "£400-£900",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "What happens if you ignore it The cost rises the longer you wait Symptom If Ignored Cost If Caught Early Cost If Ignored Ticking only Valve train wear increases £400-£900 £800-£2,000+ Ticking + low oil (ignored) Bearing wear leading to rod knock £60-£150 £800-£10,000+ Ticking + power loss Camshaft lobe flattening £1,000-£3,000 £2,500-£7,000+ The £5,000 mistake: Ignoring a ticking noise for just a few more weeks can turn a £60 oil change into a £10,000 engine replacement."
                },
                {
                  "title": "What to do next",
                  "text": "Step 1: Check your oil level (£0) Is the oil level at the correct mark? Does the oil look clean or black/sludgy? When was your last oil change? Step 2: If oil level is low Top up to the correct level. Listen for noise change. If ticking disappears → problem solved (£60-£150). Step 3: If ticking persists Book a professional diagnostic (£50-£150). A technician will identify if valve train, hydraulic lifter, or camshaft issue.",
                  "highlight": "",
